(vector (map (:db/id -1) (:adr/id 2799008321) (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-8321 — Motorcycle Drivers Dispatch/Logistics-Scheduling Coordination Coverage") (:adr/status :accepted) (:adr/date "2026-07-17") (:adr/doc_type "adr") (:adr/source-format "edn") (:adr/scope (vector :kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8321)) (:adr/references (vector 2607121000)) (:adr/body "# ADR 2799008321: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 8321 Motorcycle Drivers dispatch/logistics-scheduling coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the ISCO-08 occupation-classification track (sibling to\nthe `cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 8321\n-- Motorcycle Drivers** only.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"8321\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"8321\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Motorcycle Drivers\" -- confirming\nthe premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's `:maturity`\nwas `:spec` with `:required-technologies [:robotics :identity\n:audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`. This ADR and its\ncompanion registry edit promote the `8321` entry to `:implemented`.\n\n**Road-vehicle-operation safety dimension.** Motorcycle Drivers in this\ndomain are courier/delivery riders who directly operate a vehicle on\npublic roads. This actor is deliberately scoped to **dispatch and\nlogistics scheduling coordination ONLY -- it never operates the\nmotorcycle, and it never finalizes a route or traffic-navigation\ndecision or overrides a rider's on-road safety judgment**. Those two\nactions are a hard, permanent block in the governor, independent of\nconfidence and independent of which op was proposed -- never\nauto-commit-eligible, never merely gated behind human escalation. This\nmirrors the same class of guardrail this fleet has already applied to\nother domains with an irreversible physical/liberty/safety stake (see\ne.g. ADR-2607152500's precedent that decisions directly touching a\nperson's safety must always exclude the closed op allowlist rather\nthan merely be gated behind a confidence threshold), applied here to\nthe specific risk shape of an on-road vehicle operator: the actor may\ncoordinate the *administrative* side of dispatch (who is on shift,\nwhat delivery/incident got logged, what a maintenance order should be)\nbut must never be positioned to tell a rider what route to take, what\ntraffic decision to make, or to override the rider's own judgment\nabout their on-road safety in the moment.\n\nThis build was picked up as a retry after a prior agent run was cut off\nby a session rate limit mid-task. The prior run had already created the\nGitHub repository `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8321` (confirmed\nvia a fresh `gh repo view --json isEmpty` check to be completely empty,\nno initial commit, before any further action was taken -- so no `gh\nrepo create` was re-attempted) and had left a fully-built scaffold\nsitting in a local, never-pushed git repository in a scratch directory\nin an earlier session's scratchpad. This retry independently re-read\nevery source, test and documentation file in that scaffold in full\nagainst this ADR's own requirements before trusting and pushing it --\nconfirming, rather than assuming, that the closed op-allowlist, the\nindependently-verified-rider-provenance gate, and the phrase-based\nroute/traffic-navigation-finalization hard block were implemented\ncorrectly, and that the known self-tripping bug pattern (a\nscope-exclusion term list phrased as bare nouns like \"route\"/\"traffic\"\nmatching inside the mock advisor's own default rationale text) was\nalready fixed by phrasing every scope-exclusion term as a full\nfinalization/execution ACTION phrase (e.g. \"finalize the route\ndecision\", \"override the rider's on-road safety judgment\"), with a\ndedicated regression test\n(`motodispatch.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip`)\nproving the default mock advisor's own proposals across all four\nallowlisted ops never self-trip that check. Only after this independent\nre-verification, and a clean `clojure -M:test` run against the actual\npushed repository, does this ADR record the scaffold as accepted.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3313`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3313)\n(Accounting Associate Professionals: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/\n`actor` split, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set --\nCODE_OF_CONDUCT.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, GOVERNANCE.md, LICENSE\n(AGPL-3.0-or-later), README.md, SECURITY.md,\ndocs/business-model.md, docs/operator-guide.md), independently\nre-cloned and re-read in full in this session (local clone HEAD\n`dcae6820f78aa3ffb8a4bbf6ec37cdf44729745b`, confirmed to match\n`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3313`'s live `HEAD` via the GitHub\nAPI immediately before use).\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8321` as an OSS\ndispatch/logistics-coordination actor for independent motorcycle\ncourier/delivery dispatch practices, following the SAME governed-actor\narchitecture as every prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this\nfleet: **Motorcycle Dispatch Advisor ⊣ MotorcycleDispatchGovernor** on\na `langgraph.graph` StateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`,\ngit-sha-pinned identically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a\ndifferent library coordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the\nunrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger. `kotoba-lang/technology` is deliberately NOT a\n`deps.edn` dependency of this actor repo -- only the central\n`kotoba-lang/occupation` registry depends on it.\n\nThis actor is **dispatch/logistics-scheduling coordination ONLY,\nnever vehicle-operation authority** -- it must NEVER be designed to\nexercise, simulate exercising, or propose exercising any decision that\ndirectly finalizes a route/traffic-navigation decision or overrides a\nrider's on-road safety judgment.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-delivery-record` -- trip/delivery/incident-report data logging\n- `:schedule-dispatch-operation` -- rider-roster/route-assignment\n  scheduling proposal (an administrative scheduling proposal, never a\n  route/turn-by-turn navigation decision)\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a vehicle-defect/road-hazard/\n  rider-fatigue concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER auto-commit-eligible\n- `:coordinate-maintenance-order` -- motorcycle maintenance procurement\n  proposal\n\n`motodispatch.governor/allowed-ops` is a closed four-op `#{}` set --\nany `:op` outside it is unconditionally rejected as\n`:op-not-allowlisted` (`motodispatch.governor-test/hard-on-op-not-\nallowlisted`), and the mock advisor\n(`motodispatch.advisor/mock-advisor`) can only ever emit one of these\nfour ops (its `infer` function threads the request's own `:op` through\nunchanged, with no path to synthesize a foreign op).\n\n### Nine HARD governor checks (`motodispatch.governor/hard-violations`, permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **No client** -- the dispatch/courier operator organization\n   (`client-record`) must be independently registered; an unregistered\n   client is a HARD block (`:no-client`).\n2. **Op not allowlisted** -- any `:op` outside the closed four-op\n   allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:op-not-allowlisted`).\n3. **No actuation** -- `:effect` must be `:propose`; any other value\n   is a HARD block (`:no-actuation`) -- the governor never dispatches\n   hardware itself and never operates the motorcycle.\n4. **Unregistered rider** -- the proposal must cite a REGISTERED rider\n   (`rider-record`); a nil lookup is a HARD block\n   (`:unregistered-rider`). Never trusts the proposal's own claim of\n   who the rider is.\n5. **Rider wrong client** -- a registered rider belonging to a\n   DIFFERENT client than the requesting client is a HARD block\n   (`:rider-wrong-client`).\n6. **Rider license unverified** -- a registered rider whose\n   `:license-verified?` is not `true` is a HARD block\n   (`:rider-license-unverified`) -- this directly implements the task's\n   \"rider/license record must be independently verified/registered\n   before any action\" invariant.\n7. **Route/traffic-navigation finalization block** -- independent of\n   the op-allowlist check, any proposal whose `:rationale`/`:detail`\n   free text names a route/traffic-navigation finalization action or a\n   rider-safety-judgment override action (`motodispatch.governor/scope-\n   excluded-phrases`: \"finalize the route decision\", \"finalize a route\n   decision\", \"finalize the traffic-navigation decision\", \"finalize a\n   traffic-navigation decision\", \"override the rider's route\n   judgment\", \"override the rider's on-road safety judgment\",\n   \"override rider on-road safety judgment\", \"dispatch the vehicle\n   directly\", \"operate the motorcycle directly\") is a HARD, PERMANENT\n   block (`:route-traffic-finalization-blocked`), evaluated\n   unconditionally on content regardless of confidence or op. Full\n   action PHRASES only, deliberately never bare nouns such as \"route\"\n   or \"traffic\" -- see the self-trip guard section below.\n8. **Unknown motorcycle** -- a `:coordinate-maintenance-order`\n   proposal must cite a REGISTERED motorcycle\n   (`motorcycle-record`); a nil lookup is a HARD block\n   (`:unknown-motorcycle`).\n9. **Motorcycle wrong client** -- a registered motorcycle belonging to\n   a DIFFERENT client than the requesting client is a HARD block\n   (`:motorcycle-wrong-client`).\n\n### One always-escalate op, one cost-threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (`motodispatch.governor/always-escalate-ops`). Vehicle-\n  defect / road-hazard / rider-fatigue concerns are never\n  auto-resolved.\n- a `:coordinate-maintenance-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds the\n  registered motorcycle's `:max-maintenance-cost` ceiling always needs\n  human sign-off, independent of confidence (inclusive boundary\n  verified by `motodispatch.governor-test/ok-maintenance-order-at-\n  exact-cost-ceiling` -- exactly-at-ceiling auto-commits, one unit\n  above escalates per\n  `motodispatch.governor-test/escalates-maintenance-order-above-cost-\n  threshold`).\n- advisor confidence below `motodispatch.governor/confidence-floor`\n  (0.6) also escalates, for any op\n  (`motodispatch.governor-test/escalates-low-confidence`).\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"route\", \"traffic\") can accidentally match inside the mock advisor's\nown default rationale text for a legitimate proposal, self-blocking\nthe actor's own happy path -- exactly the risk this vertical's own\nvocabulary (every dispatch/schedule proposal necessarily mentions the\nrider and the operation) could trigger if phrased carelessly.\n`motodispatch.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is phrased exclusively\nas finalization/execution ACTIONS, never bare nouns, and\n`motodispatch.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-\ntrip` is a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor\n(`motodispatch.advisor/mock-advisor`), never trips\n`:route-traffic-finalization-blocked`. Green on this session's test\nrun -- the guard was never observed to self-trip during\nre-verification.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"8321\" ...}` entry promoted\n  from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id` set to\n  the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8321` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-8321`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary` immediately before the edit, not\n  assumed, to account for concurrent sibling agents landing changes to\n  the same registry file in this batch).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`) run against the actual pushed\n  repository: 22 tests, 49 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors -- raw\n  output captured in this ADR's `:test/counts` and in the task report.\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to this actor's own\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  depends on it.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-route-change` or\n  `:finalize-dispatch-route` that is merely gated behind\n  `always-escalate-ops` rather than structurally excluded: rejected\n  outright per the task's explicit guidance and this fleet's\n  established precedent for irreversible-safety-stake decisions -- an\n  always-escalate op still means the *capability* to finalize a route\n  or traffic-navigation decision exists in the code path and is merely\n  deferred to a human gate. This actor coordinates dispatch/logistics\n  scheduling only; the capability to finalize on-road navigation or\n  override rider safety judgment must not exist at all, hence a hard,\n  permanent, content-based block rather than an escalation gate.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"route\" \"traffic\"\n  \"navigation\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above -- this actor's own domain necessarily mentions\n  \"route\" and similar words in ordinary dispatch/schedule rationale\n  text (e.g. \"assign rider to zone-3 roster shift\"), so a bare-noun\n  list would risk self-blocking the actor's own legitimate proposals.\n  Phrased instead as full finalization/execution action phrases, with a\n  dedicated regression test proving the default advisor's own\n  proposals never self-trip.\n- A numeric confidence-only gate for `:log-delivery-record` /\n  `:schedule-dispatch-operation` / `:coordinate-maintenance-order` (no\n  rider-provenance/license-verification or route/traffic-finalization\n  content checks): rejected as insufficient -- confidence measures the\n  advisor's certainty about the proposal it chose to make, not whether\n  that proposal cites an unverified rider or smuggles a route-\n  finalization decision in its free text, which is exactly why the\n  rider-verification and scope-exclusion checks exist as independent,\n  content-based, permanent HARD blocks regardless of confidence.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-delivery-record`** -- trip/delivery/incident-report data\n   logging only. Requires an independently registered AND\n   license-verified rider (HARD-blocked otherwise by checks 4/5/6).\n   Not a route/navigation decision or vehicle-operation action in any\n   respect -- it is a records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-dispatch-operation`** -- rider-roster/route-assignment\n   *scheduling* proposal (administrative logistics, e.g. \"assign rider\n   to zone-3 roster shift\"), never a turn-by-turn route/traffic-\n   navigation decision. Any free text that names a route/traffic-\n   navigation finalization action or a rider-safety-judgment override\n   is independently HARD-blocked by check 7 regardless of what op was\n   used to carry it.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a vehicle-defect/road-\n   hazard/rider-fatigue concern to a human; ALWAYS escalates\n   (`always-escalate-ops`, unconditionally, at every confidence level),\n   NEVER auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY channel through which\n   the robot may surface a safety observation, and it explicitly never\n   resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself.\n4. **`:coordinate-maintenance-order`** -- motorcycle maintenance\n   procurement proposal. Requires an independently registered\n   motorcycle belonging to the requesting client (HARD-blocked\n   otherwise by checks 8/9), and any proposal above the registered\n   `:max-maintenance-cost` ceiling always escalates to a human,\n   independent of confidence. Not a vehicle-operation or route-\n   navigation action -- it is a purchasing-logistics action.\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase,\nfinalizes a route or traffic-navigation decision, or overrides a\nrider's on-road safety judgment -- confirmed by: (a) the closed\nfour-op allowlist itself (`motodispatch.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) the\ncontent-based, phrase-driven scope-exclusion check independent of the\n`:op` field (`motodispatch.governor/scope-excluded?`,\n`motodispatch.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`), tested directly against\n`governor/check`\n(`motodispatch.governor-test/hard-on-route-finalization-phrase-in-\nrationale`,\n`motodispatch.governor-test/hard-on-override-rider-safety-judgment-\nphrase-in-detail`), and (c) the dedicated self-trip regression proving\nthe default mock advisor's own proposals, across all four allowlisted\nops, never accidentally trip that same block\n(`motodispatch.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-\ntrip`).\n") (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-8321") (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8321") (:registry/maturity :implemented) (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)) (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)) (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-8321) (:actor/name "Independent Motorcycle Courier Dispatch Practice") (:actor/isco-08 "8321") (:actor/domain :logistics/motorcycle-dispatch) (:actor/robotics? true) (:actor/coordination? true) (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-delivery-record :schedule-dispatch-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-maintenance-order)) (:actor/hard-checks (vector :no-client :op-not-allowlisted :no-actuation :unregistered-rider :rider-wrong-client :rider-license-unverified :route-traffic-finalization-blocked :unknown-motorcycle :motorcycle-wrong-client)) (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-safety-concern)) (:actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-maintenance-order max-maintenance-cost}") (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "finalize the route decision" "finalize a route decision" "finalize the traffic-navigation decision" "finalize a traffic-navigation decision" "override the rider's route judgment" "override the rider's on-road safety judgment" "override rider on-road safety judgment" "dispatch the vehicle directly" "operate the motorcycle directly")) (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)) (:operation/entry-point :intake) (:test/counts "{:total 22, :assertions 49, :failures 0, :errors 0}") (:test/simulator :motodispatch.actor-test) (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :rider-verification :motorcycle-verification :closed-op-allowlist :maintenance-cost-threshold-escalation :route-traffic-finalization-block)) (:test/raw-output "Running tests in #{\"test\"}\n\nTesting motodispatch.actor-test\n\nTesting motodispatch.governor-test\n\nRan 22 tests containing 49 assertions.\n0 failures, 0 errors.\n")))
